            <ArticleTitle>Resolution of nebivolol-induced coronary vasospasm by intracoronary nitroglycerin during a coronary angiogram.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>825-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.repc.2012.04.016</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0870-2551(12)00224-7</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Nebivolol is a novel beta1-selective beta-blocker with vasodilator properties mediated through activation of the l-arginine-nitric oxide pathway. There is no published report of coronary artery spasm associated with nebivolol. We describe a 64-year-old female patient who developed unstable angina secondary to nebivolol-induced vasospastic angina which was also visible during coronary angiography.</AbstractText>
